From 34e25f6fad4ec0796549f7b379df05323a790ef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:31:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] apps: paper/ink Dialer main page

Squashed from:
- 0003-paper-ink-main-page
- 0004-fix-rounded-main-outlines

Change-Id: I35475f979e19826825597837fdc11275b5e727e6

Rows and borderless targets (theme selectable/list/action-bar backgrounds, bottom tabs) have no frame at rest, so adjacent views no longer double their edges; dialpad keys are separate outlined tiles (2dp inset); the dialpad sheet keeps its 28dp top corners; the selected tab is a pill with a double-width edge; the call-with-a-note card and its subject list are outlined.

Main-page edges are whole-pixel 1dp (2px at 300dpi) and active states one 2dp edge instead of a second inset ring; dashes are 3dp/2dp. Dialogs and popup menus get their edge only from the window border (FlatWindowBorder): the dialog fill has no stroke and the popup is the white native nine-patch. The progress ring is round(density) wide.
